# Supabase enhancement boundary

**Binding:** [ADR-004: Account and cloud enhancement model](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) (Accepted), [ADR-006: Serverless and secret boundary](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md) (Accepted). **Local system of record:** [ADR-002](../adrs/ADR-002-local-data-ownership.md). **Product baseline:** [ADR-001](../adrs/ADR-001-product-operating-model.md). **Sync semantics (design intent for cloud work):** [ADR-005](../adrs/ADR-005-sync-and-conflict-resolution.md) (Proposed). **Schemas at boundaries:** [ADR-008](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md). **Self-hosting direction (not binding until Accepted):** [ADR-011](../adrs/ADR-011-self-hosting-provider-model.md). **Layering:** [`src/lib/api/cloud/README.md`](../src/lib/api/cloud/README.md), [`src/lib/api/README.md`](../src/lib/api/README.md).

## What Supabase is allowed to own

- **Auth/session identity**, **account-scoped remote storage** for backup/sync/share, and **permission-backed capability checks** for those enhancements only.
- **Not** the anonymous recipe book runtime source of truth: Dexie remains primary on-device ([ADR-002](../adrs/ADR-002-local-data-ownership.md)); cloud rows are replicas/enhancements ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md), [ADR-005](../adrs/ADR-005-sync-and-conflict-resolution.md)).

## Wiring conventions

- **Server request client:** `src/hooks.server.ts` attaches `event.locals.supabase` with `@supabase/ssr`, `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, and validated session via `safeGetSession` (JWT checked with `getUser`, not session alone).
- **Universal layout client:** `src/routes/+layout.ts` builds the browser Supabase client used by loads and UI with `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`; during SSR it still creates the `@supabase/ssr` layout client required by the Supabase SvelteKit pattern, but trusted `session` / `user` data comes from `+layout.server.ts` via `locals.safeGetSession`. GAP-016 and GAP-017 in [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md) track browser verification and longer-term factory consolidation.
- **Privileged credentials:** use **only** browser-safe project keys in client and SSR client graphs; **never** import service-role or other privileged Supabase secrets into client graphs or shared modules ([ADR-006](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md)).
- **Remote recipe/cloud mutations:** prefer `CloudService` / `SyncService` under `src/lib/api/cloud/` (constructor-injected `SupabaseClient` + `userId`) rather than scattering ad hoc table access ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) enforcement). Standalone `createClient` modules (`supabaseClient.ts`, `db/remote.ts`, `api/common/common.model.ts`) should shrink over time, not multiply.

## Auth, sharing, and backup — client surfaces (legacy `agents.md` distribution)

Root [`agents.md`](../agents.md) used to summarize Supabase in two bullets (`supabaseClient.ts` for login; `locals.supabase` for route guards). **Authoritative wiring** is the table below — it supersedes that wording when they disagree.

| Surface | Role | Typical files |
| ------- | ---- | ------------- |
| **`event.locals.supabase`** | Per-request SSR client (`@supabase/ssr` `createServerClient`, `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`). Cookie-backed session; used by **`safeGetSession`**, auth **form actions** (`signInWithPassword`, `verifyOtp`, etc.), and the **`authGuard`** chain that sets `event.locals.session`, `user`, and `permissions`. | [`src/hooks.server.ts`](../src/hooks.server.ts), [`src/routes/auth/+page.server.ts`](../src/routes/auth/+page.server.ts), [`src/routes/auth/confirm/+server.ts`](../src/routes/auth/confirm/+server.ts) |
| **`data.supabase` from layout load** | Universal client: browser `createBrowserClient` or SSR branch `createServerClient` with `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`. Exposed to pages for session reads, **`CloudService` / `AccountService`**, and other layout consumers. Trusted SSR session/user values come from `+layout.server.ts`, which calls `locals.safeGetSession`; the SSR branch exists to keep the Supabase client available to layout consumers. | [`src/routes/+layout.ts`](../src/routes/+layout.ts), [`src/routes/+layout.server.ts`](../src/routes/+layout.server.ts) |
| **`src/lib/supabaseClient.ts`** | Standalone `createClient` + `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` **without** the SSR cookie adapter — **narrow** use today (e.g. share-by-token API). **Not** the primary password/OTP login path. Prefer `locals.supabase` or layout-injected clients for new auth or user-scoped cloud work. | [`src/lib/supabaseClient.ts`](../src/lib/supabaseClient.ts), [`src/routes/api/share/[token]/+server.ts`](../src/routes/api/share/%5Btoken%5D/+server.ts) |

**Backup, sync, and sharing** behavior and layering: [ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md), [`src/lib/api/cloud/README.md`](../src/lib/api/cloud/README.md). **Secrets and which keys may appear in client graphs:** [ADR-006](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md).

**Legacy discrepancy:** The old `agents.md` bullets omitted **`+layout.ts` / `data.supabase`** and implied **`supabaseClient.ts` owns “authentication at login.”** Current login flows use **`locals.supabase`**. The legacy anon-key split has been migrated to `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`; factory sprawl remains **GAP-017**, and browser verification remains tracked under **GAP-016** in [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md) and the [Supabase consolidation audit](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md#supabase-consolidation-audit-2026-05-10).

## New and changed Supabase-related work

- **Logged out / offline / missing permission:** core local recipe flows stay usable; cloud actions **degrade** (disable, defer, explain) instead of breaking unrelated UI ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) continuity).
- **Validation:** treat Supabase responses like any external I/O—validate with Zod (or equivalent) before trusting shapes ([ADR-008](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md)).
- **Provider-agnostic discipline:** avoid encoding “WFD-managed Supabase only” into **domain contracts**, shared types, or permission logic that should later admit **user-hosted** databases with the same responsibilities ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) self-hosting boundary; [ADR-011](../adrs/ADR-011-self-hosting-provider-model.md)).

